**Technical Specification Document: Utilities Sector Operations**

**Document Title:** Operational Framework for Smart Meter Integration in the Urban Utilities Network

**Date:** October 12, 2023  
**Prepared by:** James T. Caldwell, Operations Manager, Green City Utilities (GCU)  
**Reviewed by:** Sarah L. Kim, Chief Technology Officer, GCU

**1. Purpose:**  
This document outlines the operational requirements and constraints for the integration of the Advanced Metering Infrastructure (AMI) system provided by SmartTech Solutions in collaboration with the existing Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) system at GCU.

**2. Scope:**  
The integration will cover the metropolitan area of Green Valley, focusing on residential and commercial sectors. The project aims to enhance billing accuracy, reduce operational costs, and improve customer service through real-time data analytics.

**3. Requirements:**

- **3.1 Smart Meter Installation:**  
  - Engage 15 certified technicians from Electra Services for installation by December 15, 2023.
  - Installation of approximately 10,000 smart meters from MeterCorp, ensuring compliance with ANSI C12.1 standards.

- **3.2 Data Integration:**  
  - Implement a secure API connection between AMI and SCADA systems by January 5, 2024, facilitated by IT Solutions Inc.
  - Ensure compatibility with existing GIS systems managed by GeoData Systems.

- **3.3 Customer Communication:**  
  - Develop a customer notification protocol in collaboration with Public Relations, targeting 100% outreach by the end of November 2023.

**4. Constraints:**

- **4.1 Budgetary Limitations:**  
  - Total project budget capped at $1.5 million, including hardware, installation, and software costs.
  
- **4.2 Regulatory Compliance:**  
  - All operations must adhere to regulations set forth by the Public Utilities Commission of Green Valley, with periodic audits scheduled every six months.

**5. Dependencies:**

- The successful deployment of the smart meters is dependent upon timely delivery from MeterCorp, with a deadline of November 30, 2023.
- The performance of the AMI system relies on the integrity of the data processed through the SCADA system, which is currently managed by the Operations Division, led by Thomas J. Reed.

**6. Conclusion:**  
The timely execution of this operational plan is crucial for GCU to enhance service delivery and operational efficiency. Regular updates will be communicated to all stakeholders, including the Green Valley City Council and the customer advocacy group, Citizens for Energy Reform. Failure to adhere to outlined requirements and constraints may jeopardize project timelines and overall operational goals.